Run the grammars that llama.cpp generates (chat-template tool calls, a
response format next to tools) on llguidance when
common_params_sampling::grammar_llguidance is set. The GBNF is translated to
llguidance Lark at sampler creation (common/gbnf-to-lark.cpp); the lazy
triggers stay in llama.cpp code, as llama-grammar.cpp runs them. A grammar
that does not translate or compile stays on GBNF with a warning. During
generation the sampler moves to GBNF, by replaying the accepted tokens, when
llguidance fails or rejects a sampled token that GBNF accepts. The
llguidance tokenizer treats added tokens (such as <tool_call>) as special.
The one-token fast path checks the sampled token without a full mask.
User grammars are not touched. With the field off (the default), sampling is
the same as upstream except for the llguidance tokenizer and fast path, which
only matter when an llguidance grammar is in use. See PATCHES.md.

