+// LocalAI: translation of the GBNF grammars that llama.cpp generates (chat-template tool calls,
+// response formats) to the Lark dialect of llguidance, so they can run on the llguidance sampler.
+
+// True when llguidance sees the token as special: it matches the token only by id, never by its
+// text. That is a token with no text without special rendering (a control token), or an added
+// (user-defined) token such as <tool_call> in Qwen, which GBNF also treats as one unit when a
+// grammar names it with <[id]>. The llguidance tokenizer and the translation use this one test.
+bool common_llg_token_is_special(const llama_vocab * vocab, llama_token token);
+
+// Translates a GBNF grammar, as llama.cpp generates it, to llguidance Lark. The result starts with
+// "%llguidance {}" and its start rule is the GBNF rule `root`. Needs the vocab of the model when the
+// grammar names tokens or spells special tokens.
+//
+// - A rule that names no token and is not recursive becomes a Lark terminal (one lexeme).
+// - A group of rules that recurse only in tail position (the "text until a delimiter" and trigger
+//   scan automata) becomes regex terminals, with the token steps kept as rules between them.
+// - <[id]> is kept for a special token and becomes the token text otherwise. !<[id]> becomes "any
+//   character or any special token outside the set".
+// - A literal that spells a special token also accepts that token, and free text ("[^...]", ".")
+//   in a rule also accepts the special tokens the grammar does not name, except end-of-generation
+//   tokens: GBNF matches the text of such a token, llguidance only its id.
+//
+// Throws std::runtime_error on a grammar it cannot translate.
+std::string common_gbnf_to_lark(const std::string & gbnf, const llama_vocab * vocab, const std::string & root = "root");
