+// LocalAI: a llama.cpp-generated GBNF grammar (tool calls, response format) run on llguidance after
+// translation to Lark (gbnf-to-lark.h).
+//
+// - Lazy grammars keep the trigger semantics of llama-grammar.cpp: no constraint until a trigger
+//   token or pattern shows up, then the tokens from the trigger start on are replayed into
+//   llguidance (a token that starts before the trigger is tokenized again from the trigger start).
+// - The generation prompt is prefilled as plain text: llguidance checks bytes, and GBNF matches the
+//   text of a special token that the grammar does not name.
